#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""newr - the package manager for the discord-py-skills pack.

Install agent skills for building discord.py bots the way Homebrew
installs formulae:

    newr search              list every installable package
    newr install slash-commands
    newr install all         install all seven skills
    newr install starter-bot install the runnable starter bot into ./starter-bot
    newr list                show installed skills
    newr update              refresh the registry and update installed skills
    newr uninstall testing

Skills install to ~/.newr/skills/<name> by default (NEWR_HOME overrides
the prefix). Templates install into the current directory unless
--target is given.

Multi-agent install: the same skills work in every agent that reads
the open Agent Skills format (SKILL.md + frontmatter). Install them
straight into an agent's skill directory:

    newr install --agent claude-code all
    newr install --agent codex,cursor slash-commands
    newr install --agent auto all      install into every agent detected
    newr install --agent all all       install into every known agent
    newr install --agent copilot --project testing
                                       install into ./.github/skills/

Run `newr agents` to see every supported agent, its skill directory,
and which agents are detected on this machine. Aider has no skill
system, so --agent aider installs a CONVENTIONS.md digest instead.

Everything is fetched from the public repo at
https://github.com/drewdestar/discord-py-skills; no account, no token,
no build step. Python 3.10+ and the standard library only.
"""

